# MCP server

## Do

- Name server **`agent-remote-control`**; stdio transport for local Cursor/CLI.
- Implement tools: `remote.status`, `remote.notify`, `remote.request_approval`, `remote.ask_user`, `remote.checkpoint`, `remote.report_diff`, `remote.loopback_enqueue` with Zod I/O.
- Pass bridge URL/token via **environment variables**, not CLI args.
- Connect only to authenticated local bridge; return diagnostics if bridge down.
- Expose read-only resources (`agent-remote://sessions`, approvals, events) without secrets.
- Rate limit tool calls; audit approval and ask-user flows.

## Do not

- Expose arbitrary shell, file write, or network tools without approval policy.
- Embed secrets in resources or tool responses.
- Allow MCP callers to bypass Telegram pairing or approval queue.

## Prompts

Optional: `remote-safe-plan`, `remote-approval-required`, `remote-session-summary`, `remote-diff-summary`.
